  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    51.84,
    716.04,
    287.28,
    771.48
   ],
   "id": "e16",
   "lines": [
    {
     "bbox": [
      52.56,
      716.04,
      228.6,
      725.4
     ],
     "text": "Description\u2014see also comparison tables"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      51.84,
      730.08,
      287.28,
      739.08
     ],
     "text": "This variety is a late-maturing, spring type, hexaploid triticale."
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      52.56,
      741.24,
      287.28,
      749.88
     ],
     "text": "\u2018Abacus\u2019 has brown chaff, long tapering heads, strongly pig-"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      52.2,
      752.04,
      287.28,
      761.04
     ],
     "text": "mented flag leaf auricles and pubescence present on the pedun-"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      51.84,
      762.84,
      287.28,
      771.48
     ],
     "text": "cle. \u2018Abacus\u2019 has a longer head than \u2018Muir\u2019 or \u2018Tahara\u2019 and a"
    }
   ],
   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "Description\u2014see also comparison tables\nThis variety is a late-maturing, spring type, hexaploid triticale.\n\u2018Abacus\u2019 has brown chaff, long tapering heads, strongly pig-\nmented flag leaf auricles and pubescence present on the pedun-\ncle. \u2018Abacus\u2019 has a longer head than \u2018Muir\u2019 or \u2018Tahara\u2019 and a",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "type": "text"
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    315.36,
    607.68,
    551.52,
    770.76
   ],
   "id": "e17",
   "lines": [
    {
     "bbox": [
      316.08,
      607.68,
      551.52,
      616.68
     ],
     "text": "denser head with shorter awns than \u2018Currency\u2019. Unlike"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      316.8,
      618.12,
      551.16,
      627.48
     ],
     "text": "\u2018Currency\u2019 but like \u2018Muir\u2019 and \u2018Tahara\u2019, \u2018Abacus\u2019 has good"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      316.08,
      628.92,
      550.8,
      637.92
     ],
     "text": "resistance to Puccinia graminis ssp. tritici race 34-2, 12, 13."
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      315.72,
      648.36,
      342.72,
      657.36
     ],
     "text": "Origin"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      315.36,
      662.76,
      551.16,
      671.76
     ],
     "text": "The breeder is K V Cooper of the University of Adelaide, South"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      316.08,
      673.56,
      551.16,
      682.92
     ],
     "text": "Australia. \u2018Abacus\u2019 derives from a locally produced primary"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      315.72,
      684.36,
      551.16,
      694.08
     ],
     "text": "triticale topcrossed to advanced triticale varieties. The pedigree"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      315.36,
      695.52,
      550.8,
      705.24
     ],
     "text": "of \u2018Abacus\u2019 is K875/\u2018Snoopy\u2019//T2893/3/ \u2018Currency\u2019. K875"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      315.72,
      706.68,
      551.16,
      715.68
     ],
     "text": "(bread wheat), \u2018Anza\u2019/\u2018Raven\u2019//\u2018Olympic\u2019/Siete Cerros 66"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      315.36,
      717.48,
      550.8,
      727.2
     ],
     "text": "obtained from A.J. Rathjen was crossed with \u2018Snoopy\u2019 Rye,"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      315.36,
      728.64,
      550.8,
      738.0
     ],
     "text": "and amphiploids were obtained by embryo culture and"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      315.36,
      739.44,
      550.8,
      748.8
     ],
     "text": "colchicine treatment. The resulting primary triticale was"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      315.36,
      750.6,
      551.16,
      759.96
     ],
     "text": "topcrossed with T2898(BGL\"s\u201d/ARS\u2014Mexipak Mut //"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      315.36,
      761.4,
      550.08,
      770.76
     ],
     "text": "BGL\"s\u201d, entry 192 in 10th ITSN) and \u2018Currency\u2019. \u2018Abacus\u2019"
    }
   ],
   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "denser head with shorter awns than \u2018Currency\u2019. Unlike\n\u2018Currency\u2019 but like \u2018Muir\u2019 and \u2018Tahara\u2019, \u2018Abacus\u2019 has good\nresistance to Puccinia graminis ssp. tritici race 34-2, 12, 13.\nOrigin\nThe breeder is K V Cooper of the University of Adelaide, South\nAustralia. \u2018Abacus\u2019 derives from a locally produced primary\ntriticale topcrossed to advanced triticale varieties. The pedigree\nof \u2018Abacus\u2019 is K875/\u2018Snoopy\u2019//T2893/3/ \u2018Currency\u2019. K875\n(bread wheat), \u2018Anza\u2019/\u2018Raven\u2019//\u2018Olympic\u2019/Siete Cerros 66\nobtained from A.J. Rathjen was crossed with \u2018Snoopy\u2019 Rye,\nand amphiploids were obtained by embryo culture and\ncolchicine treatment. The resulting primary triticale was\ntopcrossed with T2898(BGL\"s\u201d/ARS\u2014Mexipak Mut //\nBGL\"s\u201d, entry 192 in 10th ITSN) and \u2018Currency\u2019. \u2018Abacus\u2019",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "type": "text"
  },
